  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "colored pixels in the \"mouth\" of \"Y-shaped\" sprite",
  "path": "straight line in direction pointed by the convex part (tail) on the other side of the same \"Y-shaped\" sprite",
  "dst": "stack onto tail or onto other colored pixels already stacked",
  "trajectory": "ignore colored pixels stacked out of grid",
  "type2": "transform_in_place",
  "src2": "colored pixels not in the \"mouth\" of \"Y-shaped\" sprite",
  "transform2": "disappear",
  "multi_step": "move orange pixels to sprite tail one by one"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-13 rows x 10-13 cols, bg=0
  cups: 1-3 per grid, non-overlapping bboxes (>=1 cell gap)
  cup_structure:
    border: 8-connected single-color component (5-17 pixels), unique color per cup
    shape: hollow frame converging to a single-pixel tail tip on one bbox edge and open on the opposite edge. Shapes vary widely — symmetric funnels/Ys, asymmetric Ys (one arm noticeably shorter than the other), and irregular zigzag/staircase frames all occur. Do NOT assume two equal-length arms.
    tail: one bbox edge containing exactly 1 border pixel (the spike); this is the edge from which content is ejected. Other bbox edges may have any count ≥1. (When several bbox edges happen to share count 1, the solver picks among them deterministically — see solver for the disambiguation rule.)
    bbox: 3-8 rows x 3-7 cols
    mouth_interior: the cup's hollow interior — the non-border cells lying within the frame's enclosed region. Excludes bbox corners that fall outside the frame. At least 3 cells required.
  content:
    color: single non-bg color different from own border; may match other cups' border/content
    count: 1-7 pixels scattered strictly inside mouth_interior (never in bbox corners outside the walled region)
    density: 10-45% of mouth-interior cells [observed]
  ejection_path:
    direction: outward from spike along tail direction
    clear: path from spike to grid edge must be bg (no obstacles)
    overflow: content_count may exceed available run to edge; excess is dropped
  stray_pixels: 0-1 isolated non-bg pixel, outside all cup bboxes, positioned on the mouth side of some cup (past the mouth opening in the direction opposite that cup's tail) with its perpendicular coordinate falling within that cup's extent on the tail-perpendicular axis; reuses an existing cup's border or content color
  colors: 2-5 distinct non-bg colors total; each cup uses 2 (border + content)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first — build the ejected output state, then reconstruct input
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (10-13 x 10-13) and number of cups (1-3)
    2. For each cup, pick tail_direction (U/D/L/R), border_color, content_color
    3. Build cup border converging toward the chosen tail edge
       - allow arm-length asymmetry and irregular / non-Y variants (see cup_structure.shape)
       - ensure 8-connectivity
       - ensure the tail edge has exactly 1 border pixel; mouth_interior has ≥3 cells
    4. Pick content_count in [1, min(7, len(mouth_interior))]
    5. Place ejection line: content_color pixels from spike outward, length = min(content_count, available_run)
    6. Place cups on grid ensuring non-overlap and clear ejection paths
    7. Derive input: erase ejection line, scatter content_count pixels strictly within mouth_interior
    8. Optionally add 0-1 stray pixel: pick a cup, place the pixel on its mouth side (past the mouth opening in the direction opposite the tail) with perpendicular coordinate in the cup's extent
